    "institution": null,
    "description": "The world as an egg: three cosmogonical figures including a bull pushing an egg of a table, a snake wrapped around an egg and an egg in a holder upped by a crescent. The mundane egg of Heliopolis adorned with the lunar crescent. The great golden bull, adored at Meaco, in Japan, in the attitude of butting with his horn against the egg of chaos. The agathodaimon, or good genius, symbolized by a serpent circling in its genial embrace the mundane egg. Asiatic devices allusive to the cosmogony. To his Grace the Duke of Marlborough, as a consummate judge of oriental mythology, this plate is respectf",
